From e3bc2bf110e1d0627e93c7f4640f98eeef80d3df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:48:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gates): unlock rail.tdd_intent so TDD enforcement is
 honestly toggleable (refs eda6d866)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Completes the config-honest enforcement fix: the TDD pre-commit gate now has a
real OFF switch, so `init --profile minimal` = no active enforcement end to end.

- runtime-graph.js: reclassify rail.tdd_intent from a LOCKED L1 floor to a
  default-ON toggleable rail (like rail.kernel_tracking). applyRailConfig now
  honors each rail's `locked` flag instead of rejecting every rail disable, so
  the top-level `rails:` surface accepts disabling unlocked rails while locked
  L1 rails (secret_scan, branch_protection, ...) stay a non-negotiable floor.
- adoption-profiles.js: `minimal` profile disables rail.tdd_intent via the same
  workflow.gates toggle surface `forge gate disable` uses; standard/full keep it
  ON. Bumped ADOPTION_VERSION 0.0.15 -> 0.0.16.
- AGENTS.md: document TDD as a strong default that can be turned off
  (`forge gate disable rail.tdd_intent`), honestly following config.
- Tests: locked-rail rejection repointed to a still-locked rail (secret_scan);
  new coverage that tdd_intent disables via both config surfaces and that
  minimal→disabled while standard/full→enabled.

Acceptance verified E2E: disabled→hook allows, enabled→blocks, minimal→disabled,
standard/full→enabled, post-setup `forge gate disable`→takes effect immediately.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
